#: ../../source/tutorials.rst:4
msgid "Tutorials"
msgstr "教程"

#: ../../source/tutorials.rst:7
msgid ""
"A tutorial is an **experience** that takes place under the guidance of a "
"tutor. A tutorial is always **learning-oriented**."
msgstr "**体验**——教程是在导师指导下展开的一段经历。教程永远是**面向学习**的。"

#: ../../source/tutorials.rst:10
msgid ""
"A tutorial is a *practical activity*, in which the student learns by doing "
"something meaningful, towards some achievable goal."
msgstr "教程是一种*实践活动*：学生在其中通过动手做一件有意义的事来学习，朝着某个可以"
"达到的目标前进。"

#: ../../source/tutorials.rst:12
msgid ""
"A tutorial serves the user's *acquisition* of skills and knowledge - their "
"study. Its purpose is not to help the user get something done, but to help "
"them learn."
msgstr "教程服务于用户对技能与知识的*习得*，也就是他们的学习。它的目的不是帮用户把某"
"件事做成，而是帮他们学习。"

#: ../../source/tutorials.rst:14
msgid ""
"Tutorials - learning-oriented guides that describe practical steps and are "
"intended to serve our study."
msgstr "教程——面向学习、描述实操步骤的指南，意在服务于我们的学习（学）。"

#: ../../source/tutorials.rst:18
msgid "A tutorial in other words is a lesson."
msgstr "换句话说，教程就是一堂课。"

#: ../../source/tutorials.rst:20
msgid ""
"It's important to understand that while a student will learn by doing, what "
"the student *does* is not necessarily what they *learn*. Through doing, they"
" will acquire theoretical knowledge (i.e. facts), understanding, "
"familiarity. They will learn how things relate to each other and interact, "
"and how to interact with them. They will learn the names of things, the use "
"of tools, workflows, concepts, commands. And so on."
msgstr "有一点要明白：学生固然是动手学会的，但他们*做*的事，未必就是他们*学到*的东西"
"。通过动手，他们会获得理论知识（也就是事实）、理解和熟悉感。他们会了解事物之"
"间如何关联、如何相互作用，也会了解如何与它们打交道。他们会知道事物的名称，学"
"会使用工具、工作流程、概念、命令。诸如此类。"

#: ../../source/tutorials.rst:27
msgid "The tutorial as a lesson"
msgstr "作为一堂课的教程"

#: ../../source/tutorials.rst:29
msgid ""
"A lesson entails a relationship between a teacher and a pupil. In all "
"learning of this kind, *learning takes place as the pupil applies themself "
"to tasks under the instructor's guidance*."
msgstr "一堂课意味着教师与学生之间存在一种关系。在所有这类学习中，*学生只有在导师指"
"导下投身各项任务，学习才会真正发生*。"

#: ../../source/tutorials.rst:31
msgid ""
"A lesson is a *learning experience*. In a learning experience, what matters "
"is what the learner does and what happens. By contrast, the teacher's "
"explanations and recitations of fact are far less important."
msgstr "一堂课是一种*学习体验*。在学习体验里，要紧的是学习者做了什么、发生了什么。相"
"比之下，教师的解释和对事实的复述则远没有那么重要。"

#: ../../source/tutorials.rst:33
msgid ""
"A good lesson gives the learner confidence, by showing them that they can be"
" successful in a certain skill or with a certain product."
msgstr "一堂好课给学习者信心——让他们看到，自己能在某项技能或某个产品上获得成功。"

#: ../../source/tutorials.rst:37
msgid "Obligations of the teacher"
msgstr "教师的义务"

#: ../../source/tutorials.rst:41
msgid "It's not easy being a teacher."
msgstr "当教师绝非易事。"

#: ../../source/tutorials.rst:43
msgid ""
"A lesson is a kind of contract between teacher and student, in which nearly "
"all the responsibility falls upon the teacher. The teacher has "
"responsibility for what the pupil is to learn, what the pupil will do in "
"order to learn it, and for the pupil's success. Meanwhile, the only "
"responsibility of the pupil in this contract is to be attentive and to "
"follow the teacher's directions as closely as they can. There is no "
"responsibility on the pupil to learn, understand or remember."
msgstr "一堂课是教师与学生之间的一种契约，几乎所有责任都落在教师身上。学生要学什么、"
"为学会它要做什么、以及学生能否成功，都是教师的责任。而在这份契约里，学生唯一"
"的责任就是专心，并尽可能严格地照教师的指示去做。学生没有学习、理解或记住的责"
"任。"

#: ../../source/tutorials.rst:45
msgid "At the same time, the exercise you put your pupils through must be:"
msgstr "与此同时，你让学生经历的练习必须是："

#: ../../source/tutorials.rst:47
msgid "*meaningful* - the pupil needs to have a sense of achievement"
msgstr "*有意义的*——学生需要有一种成就感"

#: ../../source/tutorials.rst:48
msgid "*successful* - the pupil needs to be able to complete it"
msgstr "*成功的*——学生需要能够完成它"

#: ../../source/tutorials.rst:49
msgid ""
"*logical* - the path that the pupil takes through it needs to make sense"
msgstr "*符合逻辑*——学生所走的路径必须说得通"

#: ../../source/tutorials.rst:50
msgid ""
"*usefully complete* - the pupil must have an encounter with all of the "
"actions, concepts and tools they need to become familiar with"
msgstr "*完整而有用*——学生必须接触到所有需要熟悉的行动、概念和工具"

#: ../../source/tutorials.rst:54
msgid "The problem of tutorials"
msgstr "教程的难题"

#: ../../source/tutorials.rst:56
msgid ""
"Tutorials are rarely done well, partly because they are genuinely difficult "
"to do well, and partly because they are not well understood. In software, "
"many products lack good tutorials, or lack tutorials completely; tutorials "
"are often conflated with how-to guides."
msgstr "教程很少做得好，部分是因为要做好它确实很难，部分是因为人们对它理解不足。在软"
"件领域，许多产品缺少好教程，或者干脆没有教程；教程常常与实践指南混为一谈。"

#: ../../source/tutorials.rst:58
msgid ""
"In an ideal lesson, the teacher is present and interacts with and responds "
"to the student, correcting their mistakes and checking their learning. In "
"documentation, none of this is possible."
msgstr "在一堂理想的课上，教师就在现场，与学生互动、回应学生，纠正他们的错误，检查他"
"们的学习。而在文档里，这一切都做不到。"

#: ../../source/tutorials.rst:62
msgid ""
"Writing and maintaining tutorials can consume a remarkable amount of effort "
"and time."
msgstr "编写和维护教程，会耗掉多得惊人的精力和时间。"

#: ../../source/tutorials.rst:64
msgid ""
"It's hard enough to put together a learning experience that meets all the "
"standards described above; in many contexts the product itself evolves "
"rapidly, meaning that all that work needs to be done again to ensure that "
"the tutorial still performs its required functions."
msgstr "要打造一段符合上述所有标准的学习体验，已经够难了；而在很多情境下，产品本身变"
"化飞快，意味着所有这些活儿都得重做一遍，才能保证教程仍然发挥它该有的作用。"

#: ../../source/tutorials.rst:66
msgid ""
"You will also often find that no other part of your documentation is subject"
" to revisions the way your tutorials are. Elsewhere in documentation, "
"changes and improvements can generally be made discretely; in tutorials, "
"where the end-to-end learning journey must make sense, they often cascade "
"through the entire story."
msgstr "你还常常会发现，文档里没有别的部分像教程那样频繁地修订。文档的其他地方，改动"
"和改进通常可以各改各的；但在教程里，从头到尾的学习旅程必须讲得通，一处改动往"
"往会一路荡开，波及整个故事。"

#: ../../source/tutorials.rst:68
msgid ""
"Finally, tutorials contain the additional complication of the distinction "
"between *what is to be learned* and *what is to be done*. Not only must the "
"creator of a tutorial have a good sense of what the user must learn, and "
"when, they must also devise a meaningful learning journey that somehow "
"delivers all that."
msgstr "最后，教程还多一层麻烦：*要学的是什么*、*要做的是什么*，这两者得区分开。教程"
"的创作者不仅要清楚用户必须学会什么、何时学会，还要设计出一段有意义的学习旅程"
"，把这一切都兜住。"

#: ../../source/tutorials.rst:74
msgid "Key principles"
msgstr "核心原则"

#: ../../source/tutorials.rst:76
msgid "A tutorial is a pedagogical problem."
msgstr "教程是一个教学问题。"

#: ../../source/tutorials.rst:78
msgid ""
"It's not an easy problem, but neither is it a mystery. The principles "
"outlined below - repetition, action, small steps, results early and often, "
"concreteness and so on - are not secrets, but they are not always well "
"understood."
msgstr "它不是个容易的问题，但也并非什么谜团。下文列出的那些原则——重复、行动、小步推"
"进、尽早且频繁地拿到结果、具体化等等——都不是什么秘密，却也没有被普遍理解。"

#: ../../source/tutorials.rst:80
msgid ""
"Still, there are straightforward, effective ways to address the problems of "
"pedagogy in practice."
msgstr "不过，在实践中解决教学问题，还是有直接而有效的办法。"

#: ../../source/tutorials.rst:84
msgid "abstraction, generalisation"
msgstr "抽象、概括"

#: ../../source/tutorials.rst:85
msgid "explanation"
msgstr "解释说明"

#: ../../source/tutorials.rst:86
msgid "choices"
msgstr "选择"

#: ../../source/tutorials.rst:87
msgid "information"
msgstr "信息"

#: ../../source/tutorials.rst:89
msgid ""
"The first rule of teaching is simply: **don't try to teach**. Your job, as a"
" teacher, is to provide the learner with an experience that will allow them "
"to learn. A teacher inevitably feels a kind of anxiety to impart knowledge "
"and understanding, but if you give into it and try to teach by telling and "
"explaining, you will jeopardise the learning experience."
msgstr "教学的第一条准则很简单：**别试图去教**。作为教师，你的职责是给学习者一段能让"
"他们学习的体验。教师总会有一种急于传授知识和理解的焦躁，但你一旦屈从于它，想"
"靠讲述和解释来教，就会毁掉这段学习体验。"

#: ../../source/tutorials.rst:91
msgid ""
"Instead, *allow learning to take place*, and trust that it will. Give your "
"learner things to *do*, through which they can learn. Only your pupil can "
"learn. Sadly, however much you desire it, you will not be able to learn for "
"your pupil. You cannot make them learn. All you can do is make it so *they* "
"can learn."
msgstr "相反，*让学习发生*，并相信它自会发生。给学习者一些事情去*做*，让他们从中学习"
"。只有你的学生才能学。遗憾的是，无论你多么渴望，都无法替你的学生去学。你没法"
"让他们学会。你所能做的，只是把学习变成可能；真正学得会的，是*他们*。"

#: ../../source/tutorials.rst:95
msgid "Show the learner where they'll be going"
msgstr "让学习者知道此行的去向"

#: ../../source/tutorials.rst:97
msgid ""
"It's important to allow the learner to form an idea of what they will "
"achieve right from the start. As well as helping to set expectations, it "
"allows them to see themselves building towards the completed goal as they "
"work."
msgstr "从一开始就让学习者对将要取得的成果有个概念，这很重要。这既有助于建立预期，也"
"让他们在做的过程中看到自己正一步步走向最终的目标。"

#: ../../source/tutorials.rst:99
msgid ""
"Providing the picture the learner needs in a tutorial can be as simple as "
"informing them at the outset: *In this tutorial we will create and deploy a "
"scalable web application. Along the way we will encounter containerisation "
"tools and services.*"
msgstr "在教程里给出学习者需要的那幅图景，可以简单到一开头就告诉他们：*本教程中，我"
"们将创建并部署一个可扩展的 Web 应用。一路上我们会遇到容器化工具与服务。*"

#: ../../source/tutorials.rst:101
msgid ""
"This is not the same as saying: *In this tutorial you will learn...* - which"
" is presumptuous and a very poor pattern."
msgstr "这和说这句话不是一回事：*在本教程中你将会学到……*——那样说显得有些自以为是，是"
"一种很糟的套路。"

#: ../../source/tutorials.rst:105
msgid "Deliver visible results early and often"
msgstr "尽早、频繁地交付可见的成果"

#: ../../source/tutorials.rst:107
msgid ""
"Your learner is probably doing new and strange things that they don't fully "
"understand. Understanding comes from being able to make connections between "
"causes and effects, so let them see the results and make the connections "
"rapidly and repeatedly. Each one of those results should be something that "
"the user can see as meaningful."
msgstr "你的学习者大概正在做一些新奇的、陌生的事情，自己还没完全弄懂。理解来自在因果"
"之间建立联系，所以要让他们看到结果，并迅速、反复地建立这种联系。每一个这样的"
"结果，都应当是用户看得出意义的东西。"

#: ../../source/tutorials.rst:109
msgid ""
"Every step the learner follows should produce a comprehensible result, "
"however small."
msgstr "学习者每走一步，都应当得出一个看得懂的结果，无论多小。"

#: ../../source/tutorials.rst:113
msgid "Maintain a narrative of the expected"
msgstr "持续叙述预期"

#: ../../source/tutorials.rst:115
msgid ""
"At every step of a tutorial, the user experiences a moment of anxiety: will "
"this action produce the correct result? Part of the work of a successful "
"tutorial is to keep providing feedback to the learner that they are indeed "
"on the right path."
msgstr "教程的每一步，用户都会经历一个焦虑的瞬间：这个行动会产生正确的结果吗？成功的"
"教程，有一部分功夫就花在不断给学习者反馈，让他们确信自己确实走在正确的路上。"

#: ../../source/tutorials.rst:117
msgid ""
"Keep up a narrative of expectations: \"You will notice that ...\"; \"After a"
" few moments, the server responds with ...\". Show the user actual example "
"output, or even the exact expected output."
msgstr "不断叙述你的预期：“你会注意到……”；“过一会儿，服务器会返回……”。向用户展示真实"
"的示例输出，甚至是精确的预期输出。"

#: ../../source/tutorials.rst:119
msgid ""
"If you know in advance what the likely signs of going wrong are, consider "
"flagging them: \"If the output doesn't show ..., you have probably forgotten"
" to ...\"."
msgstr "如果你事先知道出错通常会有哪些征兆，不妨把它们标出来：“如果输出里没有显示……"
"，你多半是忘了……”。"

#: ../../source/tutorials.rst:121
msgid ""
"It's helpful to prepare the user for possibly surprising actions: \"The "
"command will probably return several hundred lines of logs in your "
"terminal.\""
msgstr "提前让用户对可能出人意料的操作有个心理准备，会很有帮助：“这条命令大概会在你"
"的终端里返回几百行日志。”"

#: ../../source/tutorials.rst:125
msgid "Point out what the learner should notice"
msgstr "指出学习者该注意什么"

#: ../../source/tutorials.rst:127
msgid ""
"Learning requires reflection. This happens at multiple levels and depths, "
"but one of the first is when the learner  observes the signs in their "
"environment. In a lesson, a learner is typically too focused on what they "
"are doing to notice them, unless they are prompted by the teacher."
msgstr "学习需要反思。反思会在多个层面、多种深度上发生，但最先发生的一层，是学习者留"
"意到周围环境中的种种迹象。在课堂上，学习者通常太专注于手上的事，注意不到这些"
"迹象，除非老师提醒。"

#: ../../source/tutorials.rst:129
msgid ""
"Your job as teacher is to close the loops of learning by pointing things "
"out, in passing, as the lesson moves along. This can be as simple as "
"pointing out how a command line prompt changes, for example."
msgstr "作为教师，你要在课程推进的过程中顺手指点，把一处处学习回路闭合起来。这可以简"
"单到比如指一下命令行提示符的变化。"

#: ../../source/tutorials.rst:131
msgid ""
"Observing is an active part of a craft, not a merely passive one. It means "
"paying attention to the environment, a skill in itself. It's often "
"neglected."
msgstr "观察是技艺中主动的一环，而非仅仅被动的一环。它意味着对环境保持留意，这本身就"
"是一门技能。而它常常被忽视。"

#: ../../source/tutorials.rst:135
msgid "Target *the feeling of doing*"
msgstr "以*行事的感受*为目标"

#: ../../source/tutorials.rst:137
msgid ""
"In all skill or craft, the accomplished practitioner experiences a *feeling "
"of doing*, a joined-up purpose, action, thinking and result."
msgstr "*行事的感受*——在一切技能、一切技艺中，娴熟的实践者都会体验到它：目的、行动、"
"思考与结果连成一体。"

#: ../../source/tutorials.rst:139
msgid ""
"As skill develops, it flows in a confident rhythm and becomes a kind of "
"pleasure. It's the pleasure of walking, for example."
msgstr "技艺渐长，动作便以自信的节奏流动起来，成为一种愉悦——比如走路的那种愉悦。"

#: ../../source/tutorials.rst:143
msgid ""
"Pay attention to your own *feeling of doing* in your work. What is it like "
"to perform a particular operation?"
msgstr "留意你自己工作时的*行事的感受*。做某个具体操作时，那是什么感觉？"

#: ../../source/tutorials.rst:145
msgid ""
"Your learner's skill depends upon their discovering this feeling, and its "
"becoming a pleasure."
msgstr "学习者的技艺，取决于他们能否发现这份感受，并让它成为一种愉悦。"

#: ../../source/tutorials.rst:147
msgid ""
"Your challenge as the creator of a tutorial is to ensure that its tasks tie "
"together purpose and action so they become a cradle for this feeling."
msgstr "作为教程的创作者，你的挑战在于：让教程中的任务把目的与行动系为一体，成为孕育"
"这份感受的摇篮。"

#: ../../source/tutorials.rst:151
msgid "Encourage and permit repetition"
msgstr "鼓励并允许重复"

#: ../../source/tutorials.rst:153
msgid ""
"Learners will return to and repeat an exercise that gives them success, for "
"the pleasure they find in getting the expected result. Doing so reaffirms to"
" them that they can do it, and that it works."
msgstr "凡是能带来成功的练习，学习者都会一再回头去做，因为拿到预期结果让他们感到愉悦"
"。这样做会再一次向他们确认：他们做得到，而且这办法管用。"

#: ../../source/tutorials.rst:155
msgid ""
"Repetition is a key to establishing the feeling of doing; being at home with"
" that feeling is a foundational layer of learning."
msgstr "重复是建立行事的感受的关键；对这份感受习以为常，是学习的基础层。"

#: ../../source/tutorials.rst:159
msgid ""
"Repetition is not the best teacher - sometimes it's the *only* teacher."
msgstr "重复并非最好的老师——有时，唯有它才是*唯一的老师*。"

#: ../../source/tutorials.rst:161
msgid ""
"In your tutorial, try to make it possible for a particular step and result "
"to be repeated. This can be difficult, for example in operations that are "
"not reversible (making it hard to go back to a previous step) - but seek it "
"wherever you can. Watching a user follow a tutorial, you may often be amazed"
" to see how often they choose to repeat a step. They are doing it just to "
"see that the same thing really does happen again."
msgstr "在你的教程里，尽量让某一步骤及其结果能够被重复。这有时并不容易，比如在不可逆"
"的操作中（很难退回上一步）——但只要找得到机会，就去找。看着用户跟着教程做，你"
"常会惊讶地发现，他们选择重复某一步的频率有多高。他们这么做，只是想亲眼看到同"
"一件事真的又发生了一次。"

#: ../../source/tutorials.rst:165
msgid "Ruthlessly minimise explanation"
msgstr "毫不留情地精简解释"

#: ../../source/tutorials.rst:167
msgid ""
"*A tutorial is not the place for explanation.* In a tutorial, the user is "
"focused on correctly following your directions and getting the expected "
"results. *Later*, when they are ready, they will seek explanation, but right"
" now they are concerned with *doing*. Explanation distracts their attention "
"from that, and blocks their learning."
msgstr "*教程不是做解释说明的地方*。在教程里，用户正专注于正确跟从你的指示、拿到预期"
"的结果。*稍后*，等他们准备好了，自会去寻求解释说明；但此刻，他们在意的是*做*"
"。解释说明会把他们的注意力从这件事上引开，阻碍他们学习。"

#: ../../source/tutorials.rst:169
msgid ""
"For example, it's quite enough to say something like: *We're using HTTPS "
"because it's more secure.* There is a place for extended discussion and "
"explanation of HTTPS, but not now. Instead, provide a link or reference to "
"that explanation, so that it's available, but doesn't get in the way."
msgstr "比如，这样说就足够了：*我们用 HTTPS，因为它更安全*。关于 HTTPS 的长篇讨论和"
"解释自有它的去处，但不是现在。改为提供一条链接或参考指向那段解释，让它随手可"
"取，又不挡路。"

#: ../../source/tutorials.rst:173
msgid ""
"Explanation is only pertinent at the moment the *user* wants it. It is not "
"for the documentation author to decide."
msgstr "解释，只在*用户*想要它的那一刻才切题。这不是文档作者该决定的事。"

#: ../../source/tutorials.rst:175
msgid ""
"Explanation is one of the hardest temptations for a teacher to resist; even "
"experienced teachers find it difficult to accept that their students' "
"learning does not depend on explanation. This is perfectly natural. Once we "
"have grasped something, we rely on the power of abstraction to frame it to "
"ourselves - and that's how we want to frame it to others. Understanding "
"means grasping general ideas, and abstraction is the logical form of "
"understanding - but these are not what we need in a tutorial, and it's not "
"how successful learning or teaching works."
msgstr "解释是教师最难抗拒的诱惑之一；即便是经验丰富的教师，也难以接受学生的学习并不"
"依赖解释。这再自然不过。一旦我们弄懂了什么，就会借助抽象的力量在心里把它框定"
"成形——而我们想展示给别人的，也正是这个样子。理解意味着把握一般的观念，抽象则"
"是理解的逻辑形式——但这些并不是教程里需要的东西，成功的学习或教学也不靠这个。"

#: ../../source/tutorials.rst:177
msgid ""
"One must see it for oneself, to see the focused attention of a student "
"dissolve into air, when a teacher's well-intentioned explanation breaks the "
"magic spell of learning."
msgstr "人非得亲眼见到，才能看到学生的专注如何顷刻化为乌有——就在教师一番好意的解释打"
"破学习的魔法之时。"

#: ../../source/tutorials.rst:181
msgid "... and focus on the concrete"
msgstr "……并聚焦于具体"

#: ../../source/tutorials.rst:183
msgid ""
"In a learning situation, your student is in the moment, a moment composed of"
" concrete things. You are responsible for setting up and maintaining the "
"student's flow, from one concrete action and result to another."
msgstr "在学习情境中，你的学生身处当下，而当下由一件件具体事物构成。你的责任是营造并"
"维持学生的流畅感，让他从一个具体的行动与结果，走向下一个。"

#: ../../source/tutorials.rst:185
msgid ""
"Focus on *this* problem, *this* action, *this* result, in such a way that "
"you lead the learner from step to concrete step."
msgstr "*这个问题*、*这个行动*、*这个结果*——聚焦于此，从而领着学习者从一个具体步骤走"
"向下一个。"

#: ../../source/tutorials.rst:187
msgid ""
"It might seem that by maintaining focus on the concrete and particular that "
"you deny the student the opportunity to see or grasp the larger general "
"patterns, but the contrary is true. The one thing our minds do spectacularly"
" well is to perceive general patterns from concrete examples. All learning "
"moves in one direction: from the concrete and particular, towards the "
"general and abstract. The latter *will* emerge from the former."
msgstr "你也许会以为，一直盯住具体和个别，就剥夺了学生看到或把握更宏大的普遍模式的机"
"会；事实恰恰相反。我们的大脑有一件事做得极其漂亮：从具体的例子中看出普遍的模"
"式。一切学习都朝着同一个方向走：从具体、个别，通向普遍、抽象。后者*终将*从前"
"者之中生长出来。"

#: ../../source/tutorials.rst:191
msgid "Ignore options and alternatives"
msgstr "忽略选项与替代方案"

#: ../../source/tutorials.rst:193
msgid ""
"Your job is to guide the learner to a successful conclusion. There may be "
"many interesting diversions along the way (different options for the command"
" you're using, different ways to use the API, different approaches to the "
"task you're describing) - ignore them. *Your guidance needs to remain "
"focused on what's required to reach the conclusion*, and everything else can"
" be left for another time."
msgstr "你的职责，是把学习者一路引向成功的结局。一路上可能有许多有趣的岔路（你在用的"
"命令还有别的选项，使用 API 还有别的路子，你要讲的任务还有别的做法）——忽略它"
"们。*你的指引必须始终聚焦在抵达终点所必需的东西上*，其余一切都可以留到以后。"

#: ../../source/tutorials.rst:195
msgid ""
"Doing this helps keep your tutorial shorter and crisper, and saves both you "
"and the reader from having to do extra cognitive work."
msgstr "这样做能让你的教程更简短、更利落，也省得你和读者多做额外的脑力活。"

#: ../../source/tutorials.rst:199
msgid "Aspire to perfect reliability"
msgstr "追求完美的可靠性"

#: ../../source/tutorials.rst:201
msgid ""
"All of the above are general principles of pedagogy, but there is a special "
"burden on the creator of a tutorial."
msgstr "以上都是教学的一般原则，但教程的创作者还背着一副特别的担子。"

#: ../../source/tutorials.rst:203
msgid ""
"A tutorial must inspire confidence. Confidence can only be built up layer by"
" layer, and is easily shaken. At every stage, when you ask your student to "
"do something, they must see the result you promise. A learner who follows "
"your directions and doesn't get the expected results will quickly lose "
"confidence, in the tutorial, the tutor and themselves."
msgstr "教程必须能让人生出信心。信心只能一层一层垒起来，却极易动摇。每一个阶段，你让"
"学生做什么，他们都必须看到你许诺的结果。学习者照着你的指示做，却没拿到预期的"
"结果，很快就会失去信心——对教程、对导师、也对自己。"

#: ../../source/tutorials.rst:207
msgid "You are required to be present, but condemned to be absent."
msgstr "要求你在场，却注定缺席。"

#: ../../source/tutorials.rst:209
msgid ""
"A teacher who's there with the learner can rescue them when things go wrong."
" In a tutorial, you can't do that. Your tutorial ought to be so well "
"constructed that things *can't* go wrong, that your tutorial works for every"
" user, every time."
msgstr "教师陪在学习者身边，出了岔子还能救一把。在教程里，你做不到。你的教程应当构造"
"得如此严密：事情*不可能*出错，对每一位用户、每一次，它都管用。"

#: ../../source/tutorials.rst:211
msgid ""
"It's hard work to create a reliable experience, but that is what you must "
"aspire to in creating a tutorial."
msgstr "打造一份可靠的体验是件苦功夫，但编写教程时，这正是你必须追求的目标。"

#: ../../source/tutorials.rst:213
msgid ""
"Your tutorial will have flaws and gaps, however carefully it is written. You"
" won't discover them all by yourself, you will have to rely on users to "
"discover them for you. The only way to learn what they are is by finding out"
" what actually happens when users do the tutorial, through extensive testing"
" and observation."
msgstr "无论教程写得多仔细，总会有缺陷和漏洞。你没法一个人把它们全找出来，只能靠用户"
"替你发现。想知道它们是什么，唯一的办法是通过大量的测试和观察，弄清用户真的照"
"着教程做时会发生什么。"

#: ../../source/tutorials.rst:219
msgid "The language of tutorials"
msgstr "教程的语言"

#: ../../source/tutorials.rst:221
msgid "We ..."
msgstr "我们……"

#: ../../source/tutorials.rst:222
msgid ""
"The first-person plural affirms the relationship between tutor and learner: "
"you are not alone; we are in this together."
msgstr "第一人称复数确认了导师与学习者之间的关系：你并不孤单；这件事我们一起做。"

#: ../../source/tutorials.rst:223
msgid "In this tutorial, we will ..."
msgstr "在本教程中，我们将……"

#: ../../source/tutorials.rst:224
msgid "Describe what the learner will accomplish."
msgstr "说明学习者将达成什么。"

#: ../../source/tutorials.rst:225
msgid "First, do x. Now, do y. Now that you have done y, do z."
msgstr "先做 x。现在做 y。既然做完了 y，就做 z。"

#: ../../source/tutorials.rst:226
msgid "No room for ambiguity or doubt."
msgstr "不留一丝含糊或怀疑的余地。"

#: ../../source/tutorials.rst:227
msgid ""
"We must always do x before we do y because... (see Explanation for more "
"details)."
msgstr "我们必须先做 x 再做 y，因为……（详见“解释说明”）。"

#: ../../source/tutorials.rst:228
msgid ""
"Provide minimal explanation of actions in the most basic language possible. "
"Link to more detailed explanation."
msgstr "用最基础的语言，对行动做最低限度的解释说明。链接到更详细的解释说明。"

#: ../../source/tutorials.rst:229
msgid "The output should look something like ..."
msgstr "输出应该大致像这样……"

#: ../../source/tutorials.rst:230
msgid "Give your learner clear expectations."
msgstr "给学习者明确的预期。"

#: ../../source/tutorials.rst:231
msgid "Notice that ... Remember that ... Let's check ..."
msgstr "注意……记住……我们来检查一下……"

#: ../../source/tutorials.rst:232
msgid ""
"Give your learner plenty of clues to help confirm they are on the right "
"track and orient themselves."
msgstr "给学习者足够多的线索，帮他们确认自己走对了路，也帮他们找准方位。"

#: ../../source/tutorials.rst:233
msgid "You have built a secure, three-layer hylomorphic stasis engine..."
msgstr "你已经构建了一台安全的三层质形静态引擎……"

#: ../../source/tutorials.rst:234
msgid ""
"Describe (and admire, in a mild way) what your learner has accomplished."
msgstr "描述（并温和地赞赏）学习者取得的成就。"

#: ../../source/tutorials.rst:240
msgid "Applied to food and cooking"
msgstr "应用于食物与烹饪"

#: ../../source/tutorials.rst:242
msgid "A child proudly showing a dish he has helped prepare"
msgstr "一个孩子自豪地展示他帮忙做好的菜"

#: ../../source/tutorials.rst:245
msgid ""
"Someone who has had the experience of teaching a child to cook will "
"understand what matters in a tutorial, and just as importantly, the things "
"that don't matter at all."
msgstr "教过孩子做饭的人，会明白教程里什么要紧；同样重要的是，也明白什么根本不要紧。"

#: ../../source/tutorials.rst:247
msgid ""
"It really doesn't matter what the child makes, or how correctly they do it. "
"The value of a lesson lies in what the child gains, not what they produce."
msgstr "孩子做出什么，做得对不对，其实都无所谓。一堂课的价值，在于孩子得到了什么，而"
"不在于他做出了什么。"

#: ../../source/tutorials.rst:249
msgid ""
"Success in a cooking lesson with a child is not the culinary outcome, or "
"whether the child can now repeat the processes on their own. Success is when"
" the child acquires the knowledge and skills you were hoping to impart."
msgstr "跟孩子上烹饪课，成功不在于最后做出什么菜，也不在于孩子从此能不能自己重复那些"
"流程。成功，是孩子真的学到了你希望传授的知识和技能。"

#: ../../source/tutorials.rst:251
msgid ""
"It's a crucial condition of this that the child discovers pleasure in the "
"experience of being in the kitchen with you, and wants to return to it. "
"Learning a skill is never a once and for all matter. Repetition is always "
"required."
msgstr "这里的一个关键条件是：孩子要从和你一起待在厨房里的经历中发现乐趣，并且愿意再"
"回来。学一门技能，从来不是“一劳永逸”的事。重复永远少不了。"

#: ../../source/tutorials.rst:253
msgid ""
"Meanwhile, the cooking lesson might be framed around the idea of learning "
"how to prepare a particular dish, but what we actually need the child to "
"learn might be things like: *that we wash our hands before handling food*; "
"*how to hold a knife*; *why the oil must be hot*; *what this utensil is "
"called*, *how to time and measure things*."
msgstr "与此同时，烹饪课或许是围绕“学做某道菜”来搭框架的，但我们真正需要孩子学的，可"
"能是这些：*碰食物之前要先洗手*；*怎么握刀*；*为什么油一定要热*；*这件器具叫"
"什么*，*怎么把握时间和分量*。"

#: ../../source/tutorials.rst:255
msgid ""
"The child learns all this by working alongside you in the kitchen; in its "
"own time, at its own pace, **through the activities** you do together, and "
"not from the things you say or show."
msgstr "孩子是在厨房里和你并肩干活时学会这一切的：按他自己的时间、自己的节奏，**通过"
"你们一起做的活动**，而不是靠你说的话或展示的东西。"

#: ../../source/tutorials.rst:257
msgid ""
"With a young child, you will often find that the lesson suddenly has to end "
"before you'd completed what you set out to do. This is normal and expected; "
"children have short attention spans. But as long as the child managed to "
"achieve something - however small - and enjoyed doing it, it will have laid "
"down something in the construction of its technical expertise, that can be "
"returned to and built upon next time."
msgstr "跟年幼的孩子在一起，你常会发现，还没做完原打算做的事，课就不得不突然结束了。"
"这很正常，也在意料之中；孩子的注意力本来就短。但只要孩子做成了点什么——无论多"
"小——而且做得开心，他就为自己的技术能力添上了一块砖，下次可以回到这里继续往上"
"垒。"
